# ffmpeg for Mandarin OS (os/ffmpeg/build.sh, item 389): all of ffmpeg's own codecs, formats, filters and protocols,
# as Debian's has them, without the video, GPU and speech libraries Debian's build links (LLVM, Mesa, Vulkan, x265,
# SVT-AV1, codec2, flite, libplacebo and more, about 300 MB that Mandarin never uses). Of the libraries outside ffmpeg,
# only those Mandarin uses: soxr (its resampling), Opus and LAME (what it encodes), GnuTLS (streams over https),
# FreeType, HarfBuzz and fontconfig (drawtext: the titles on the covers Mandarin draws, in fontconfig's sans-serif),
# zlib and bzip2. Its device library stays for lavfi (Mandarin makes silence
# and draws covers with it), with no device of its own linked. Mandarin's whole test suite runs against this build
# before an image takes it (.github/workflows/os-image.yml), and caught lavfi's absence when it was left out.
--disable-autodetect
--disable-doc
--disable-debug
--disable-static
--enable-shared
--disable-postproc
--disable-vulkan
--disable-hwaccels
--enable-libsoxr
--enable-libopus
--enable-libmp3lame
--enable-gnutls
--enable-libfreetype
--enable-libharfbuzz
--enable-libfontconfig
--enable-zlib
--enable-bzlib
--enable-iconv
--enable-pthreads
